                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 91.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 302.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 8, 1870</date>. (Received November 9,
                        1870.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose you herewith
                    certain proceedings of meetings held by the diplomatic corps, which may be taken
                    in connection with my dispatch No. 301, under date of the 4th instant, and which
                    are in a measure explanatory thereof.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>




